        "original_id": "18ec7865-aef0-5e71-b358-d77ff06f2bc7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Francisco Antonio Zea, Simón Bolívar\n- Roles: Vice President of Colombia, President of Colombia, journalist, botanist, diplomat, politician, statesman, military leader, political leader\n- Places: Colombia, Venezuela, Bolivia, Ecuador, Peru, Panama, Spanish rule\n\nFacts:\n- Francisco Antonio Zea was born on 23 November 1766 and died on 28 November 1822.\n- Simón Bolívar was born on 24 July 1783 and died on 17 December 1830.\n- Francisco Antonio Zea was a Colombian journalist, botanist, diplomat, politician, and statesman.\n- Francisco Antonio Zea served as the 1st Vice President of Colombia under President Simón Bolívar.\n- Simón Bolívar was a Venezuelan military and political leader.\n- Simón Bolívar was generally known as Simón Bolívar and colloquially as El Libertador.\n- Simón Bolívar played a leading role in the establishment of Venezuela, Bolivia, Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, and Panama as sovereign states independent of Spanish rule.",
